g.ns29:text:
\begin{minipage}{8cm}
Expands the receptive field: after MaxPool, each pixel "see" an area of the original image that is twice as large. 
\begin{itemize}
\item it enables the deep layers to understand the nanoparticle's overall structure, rather than just neighboring pixels,
\item it allows stacking a large number of filters ($\rightarrow$~256) without causing a memory explosion.
\end{itemize}
\end{minipage}

\begin{minipage}{8cm}
$$\mathrm{skip\ } C1 = C2 + C5$$

The addition merges two sources of information:

\begin{itemize}
\item $C2$: what the decoder reconstructed by working back up from the bottleneck - an abstract, global view
\item $C5$: what the encoder had captured at this level - fine details at $32\times 32$ resolution

Without this addition, the decoder would have lost the fine spatial details that were lost during the successive MaxPool operations.
\end{itemize}
\end{minipage}
